如果你看到14分14秒，就在凯文说完“男人树把它的阴茎”之后，

741
00:37:27.080 --> 00:37:30.520
it cuts to an overshoulder shot and you see her shoulders shaking.
镜头切到了过肩镜头，你可以看到她的肩膀在颤抖。

742
00:37:30.840 --> 00:37:32.860
We all thought that line was really funny.
我们都觉得那句台词特别好笑。

743
00:37:33.080 --> 00:37:34.700
I remember doing that one.
我记得那场戏是我演的。

744
00:37:34.700 --> 00:37:36.680
So Dwight has left.
所以德怀特离开了。

745
00:37:36.940 --> 00:37:38.000
He's bailed.
他溜了。

746
00:37:38.080 --> 00:37:41.980
And now they're trying to figure out how do we coax this code out of him?
现在他们正试图想办法怎么从他嘴里套出密码？

747
00:37:42.120 --> 00:37:44.040
How do we get him to stop this?
怎么让他停下这一切？

748
00:37:44.420 --> 00:37:48.760
It's going to involve Andy, Pam, Aaron, and Kevin going to Shroot FarMs.
这需要安迪、帕姆、亚伦和凯文一起去施鲁特农场。

749
00:37:49.020 --> 00:37:52.660
They come upon him and he is digging a giant hole.
他们找到他时，他正在挖一个巨大的坑。

750
00:37:52.900 --> 00:37:55.220
It turns out it's a grave for a horse.
原来那是给一匹马挖的坟墓。

751
00:37:55.460 --> 00:37:56.740
How did you get through that?
你是怎么忍住没笑场的？

752
00:37:56.940 --> 00:37:59.700
I would have laughed so hard the minute he says,
要是我的话，他一开口我就得笑喷了，

753
00:37:59.920 --> 00:38:02.960
and if you hit something, it's probably another horse.
而且如果你撞到了什么东西，那多半是另一匹马。

754
00:38:02.960 --> 00:38:05.300
If you hit another horse, you've dug too far.
如果你撞到了另一匹马，说明你挖得太深了。

755
00:38:05.380 --> 00:38:06.160
Yeah, exactly.
没错，就是这样。

756
00:38:06.620 --> 00:38:08.820
Well, lady, we did not get through this scene.
好吧，女士，我们当时确实没能顺利拍完这场戏。

757
00:38:08.980 --> 00:38:09.980
It was so funny.
太搞笑了。

758
00:38:09.980 --> 00:38:15.460
I had instant memories of it when I watched it again because there were also alts.
重看的时候我立刻就想起来了，因为当时还拍了备选方案。

759
00:38:15.860 --> 00:38:19.400
In addition to getting what you saw on the screen, we also had to shoot this.
除了你们在屏幕上看到的那些，我们还得拍这个。

760
00:38:19.600 --> 00:38:22.260
Pam says, oh, no, your horse died.
帕姆说，噢，不，你的马死了。

761
00:38:23.100 --> 00:38:24.820
And Dwight said, no.
德怀特说，不。

762
00:38:25.300 --> 00:38:30.720
If you wait for the horse to die, the corpse is sitting out for days for the other animals to see.
如果你等着马自然死亡，那尸体得在那儿放好几天，让其他动物看见。

763
00:38:30.720 --> 00:38:33.620
Once the animals know about death, it's all over.
一旦动物们知道了死亡这回事，一切就全完了。

764
00:38:34.320 --> 00:38:35.840
We couldn't get through that.
我们当时根本拍不下去。

765
00:38:36.040 --> 00:38:39.760
And another one was when Pam said, oh, no, your horse died.
还有一个版本是帕姆说，噢，不，你的马死了。

766
00:38:40.020 --> 00:38:44.140
Dwight said, no, I'm trying to trap some horse grave robbers.
德怀特说，不，我是在设陷阱抓那些盗马贼。

767
00:38:44.780 --> 00:38:45.380
What?
什么？

768
00:38:45.380 --> 00:38:49.240
So he was digging a fake horse grave as a trap.
所以他是在挖一个假马坟作为陷阱。

769
00:38:49.720 --> 00:38:50.800
Oh, my goodness.
天哪。

770
00:38:51.520 --> 00:38:54.640
Well, I'll tell you guys, we shot this out at Disney Ranch.
我告诉你们吧，我们是在迪士尼牧场拍的这场戏。

771
00:38:54.860 --> 00:38:59.300
And we actually shot this the Friday before we shot Garden Party.
而且我们是在拍《花园派对》的前一个周五拍的这场戏。

772
00:38:59.540 --> 00:39:06.740
And Steve Burgess says the reason the camera never really pans very far to the left of Dwight's farmhouse
史蒂夫·伯吉斯说，摄像机之所以从来没有大幅度向德怀特农舍的左侧平移，

773
00:39:06.740 --> 00:39:10.500
is because they had already started setting up the tent for Garden Party.
是因为他们当时已经开始为《花园派对》搭建帐篷了。

774
00:39:10.520 --> 00:39:12.300
And we had to keep it out of frame.
我们必须得把它挡在镜头之外。

775
00:39:12.760 --> 00:39:17.000
We had a very limited, like, shooting area because we were already in prep.
我们的拍摄区域非常有限，因为我们已经在做准备工作了。

776
00:39:17.000 --> 00:39:21.660
Well, while you guys are all at Shroot Farms trying to talk Dwight into giving you the passcode,
好吧，当你们都在施鲁特农场试图说服德怀特告诉你们密码时，

777
00:39:21.980 --> 00:39:26.560
Jim has been sent on assignment to keep Robert California busy and not looking at his phone
吉姆被派去执行任务，要缠住罗伯特·加州，让他没空看手机，

778
00:39:26.560 --> 00:39:30.380
so he doesn't notice if he gets emails, right, at 5 o'clock.
这样他就不会注意到五点钟有没有收到邮件了，对吧。

779
00:39:30.620 --> 00:39:34.800
And the task is go play squash with Robert California.
任务就是去和罗伯特·加州打壁球。

780
00:39:35.140 --> 00:39:38.980
Aaron is like he's somewhere either eating squash or playing squash.
亚伦说他要么是在吃壁球，要么是在打壁球。

781
00:39:39.320 --> 00:39:41.160
So Jim is on the case.
所以吉姆接下了这个任务。

782
00:39:41.340 --> 00:39:45.920
There was actually a deleted Jim talking head where he shares how much he knows about squash.
其实还有一段被删减的吉姆访谈，他在里面分享了自己对壁球的了解程度。

783
00:39:45.920 --> 00:39:47.120
And I want you to hear it.
我想让你们听听。

784
00:39:48.040 --> 00:39:51.440
I have never played squash, but I've seen it in countless 80s movies.
我从没打过壁球，但我看过无数部80年代的电影。

785
00:39:51.560 --> 00:39:55.240
And it seems like the most common mistake is that you serve too hard and hit yourself right in the squash balls.
最常见的错误似乎就是发球太用力，结果直接打到了自己的壁球蛋蛋上。

786
00:39:55.480 --> 00:39:58.120
So as long as I don't do that, I think I'll be all right.
所以只要我不犯那个错，我想我应该没问题。

787
00:39:59.980 --> 00:40:01.620
That's a very funny talking head.
那段访谈太搞笑了。

788
00:40:01.820 --> 00:40:03.380
That's all he knows about squash.
那就是他对壁球的所有了解了。

789
00:40:03.740 --> 00:40:07.040
And when he arrives, he's actually ripping the tag off his racket.
当他到达时，他其实正在撕掉球拍上的标签。

790
00:40:07.360 --> 00:40:12.620
He's clearly never played, although he tells Robert California, like, hey, I play all the time.
他显然从没打过，尽管他告诉罗伯特·加州说，嘿，我经常打。

791
00:40:12.620 --> 00:40:16.100
It starts a very funny runner between the two of them.
这开启了他们两人之间一段非常有趣的连贯剧情。

792
00:40:16.200 --> 00:40:19.340
And lady, I have a little digital clutter to share here.
女士，我这里有一点数字杂物要分享。

793
00:40:19.620 --> 00:40:20.180
Oh, yeah?
噢，是吗？

794
00:40:20.680 --> 00:40:21.240
Yeah.
是的。

795
00:40:21.680 --> 00:40:24.880
You and I did not work on the squash shoot days.
你和我当时没参与壁球那几天的拍摄。

796
00:40:25.300 --> 00:40:25.780
Okay.
好的。

797
00:40:26.240 --> 00:40:27.240
Guess what we were doing.
猜猜我们在干什么。

798
00:40:27.520 --> 00:40:28.980
I have no idea.
我完全不知道。

799
00:40:29.360 --> 00:40:29.660
Okay.
好的。

800
00:40:30.080 --> 00:40:31.380
You emailed me.
你给我发了邮件。

801
00:40:31.520 --> 00:40:35.200
Hey, lady, if I'm not totally wrecked by shooting at Shrute Farms,
嘿，女士，如果我在舒鲁特农场拍摄时没被彻底折腾垮的话，

802
00:40:35.300 --> 00:40:38.980
I'll come over tomorrow on our day off and grab the bassinet from you.
明天我们休息的时候，我会过去把你那里的摇篮拿走。

803
00:40:38.980 --> 00:40:40.400
I can't wait to see you.
我迫不及待想见你了。

804
00:40:40.500 --> 00:40:42.240
And maybe I can even see Isabel.
也许我还能见到伊莎贝尔。

805
00:40:43.200 --> 00:40:44.660
Yes, that's right.
是的，没错。

806
00:40:44.700 --> 00:40:49.640
You let me borrow this beautiful white wicker bassinet.
你借给了我这个漂亮的白色柳条摇篮。

807
00:40:50.080 --> 00:40:50.500
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

808
00:40:51.160 --> 00:40:52.720
Oh, I remember that.
哦，我记得那个。

809
00:40:52.960 --> 00:40:57.940
I was so happy that someone else could use it because it was such a beautiful gift that I got when Isabel was born.
我当时很高兴有人能用上它，因为这是伊莎贝尔出生时我收到的非常精美的礼物。

810
00:40:58.180 --> 00:41:03.060
Our family members went in together and bought us this beautiful white wicker bassinet,
我们的家人凑钱给我们买了这只漂亮的白色柳条摇篮，

811
00:41:03.180 --> 00:41:06.440
the kind that, you know, you can, it has handles and you can take it off
那种，你知道的，它有把手，你可以把它取下来，

812
00:41:06.440 --> 00:41:09.020
or you can put it on the bass and kind of roll it through the house.
或者把它放在底座上，在屋子里推着走。

813
00:41:09.240 --> 00:41:10.380
I remember that.
我记得那个。

814
00:41:10.540 --> 00:41:11.820
We kept it up in our kitchen.
我们把它放在厨房里。

815
00:41:12.100 --> 00:41:12.780
I know.
我知道。

816
00:41:12.860 --> 00:41:13.820
It made me so happy.
它让我感到非常开心。

817
00:41:14.420 --> 00:41:19.920
So back at Shrute Farms, everyone has helped Dwight dig his horse grave.
回到舒鲁特农场，大家都在帮德怀特挖马的坟墓。

818
00:41:20.580 --> 00:41:21.680
And they're tired.
他们都累坏了。

819
00:41:21.680 --> 00:41:24.600
And Pam asked if they can come inside for a little water.
帕姆问他们能不能进屋喝点水。

820
00:41:24.820 --> 00:41:29.140
She's going to talk about how, oh, I forgot how pretty it was in here.
她会说，哦，我忘了这里面有多漂亮了。

821
00:41:29.180 --> 00:41:30.140
It's so lovely.
真是太可爱了。

822
00:41:30.760 --> 00:41:32.340
And they're going to sit down.
然后他们会坐下来。

823
00:41:32.500 --> 00:41:34.760
He's going to serve them some cabbage pie.
他会给他们端上一些卷心菜派。

824
00:41:35.480 --> 00:41:39.300
And they're having this pie and making small talk.
他们吃着派，闲聊着。

825
00:41:39.460 --> 00:41:45.540
And I don't know if you noticed, but over Dwight's shoulder, there's a bit where Kevin comes out of the kitchen
我不知道你有没有注意到，在德怀特的肩膀后面，有一段凯文从厨房走出来的戏，

826
00:41:45.540 --> 00:41:47.360
and he's holding a frying pan.
他手里拿着一个煎锅。

827
00:41:47.540 --> 00:41:54.300
How can you not notice that Kevin is going to pretend to maybe whack Dwight with a frying pan?
你怎么可能没注意到凯文假装要用煎锅敲德怀特的头呢？

828
00:41:54.300 --> 00:42:02.680
Kevin, Danny said that the first frying pan they gave to Kevin was the largest frying pan anyone had ever seen.
凯文，丹尼说他们给凯文的第一个煎锅是大家见过最大的煎锅。

829
00:42:02.800 --> 00:42:04.840
He said it was like two feet in diameter.
他说直径大概有两英尺。

830
00:42:05.840 --> 00:42:10.020
And that he and Troy were like, no, no, no, just a normal frying pan.
他和特洛伊当时就说，不，不，不，只要一个普通的煎锅就行。

831
00:42:10.440 --> 00:42:11.980
And they had to switch it out.
于是他们不得不把它换掉。

832
00:42:12.600 --> 00:42:14.740
I have two things to share about this.
关于这一点，我有两件事要分享。

833
00:42:14.860 --> 00:42:17.520
First of all, I wanted to see what it said in the shooting draft.
首先，我想看看拍摄剧本里是怎么写的。

834
00:42:17.700 --> 00:42:18.800
It said this.
上面是这么写的。

835
00:42:19.040 --> 00:42:20.940
Kevin creeps in from off screen.
凯文从屏幕外悄悄走进来。

836
00:42:20.940 --> 00:42:23.540
He's got a big cast iron skillet in his hands.
他手里拿着一个大铸铁平底锅。

837
00:42:23.540 --> 00:42:26.160
He lifts it over Dwight's head to smash him.
他把它举过德怀特的头顶，想要砸下去。

838
00:42:26.520 --> 00:42:27.580
Pam shakes her head.
帕姆摇了摇头。

839
00:42:27.960 --> 00:42:28.520
No.
不。

840
00:42:29.080 --> 00:42:31.780
Kevin sets the skillet down and rejoins the table.
凯文放下平底锅，重新回到桌边。

841
00:42:32.400 --> 00:42:36.280
Well, this got me very curious about why Kevin would do this.
好吧，这让我很好奇凯文为什么要这么做。

842
00:42:36.420 --> 00:42:38.240
Why is he acting so odd?
他为什么表现得这么奇怪？

843
00:42:38.380 --> 00:42:41.060
And I found more nuggets in the shooting draft.
我在拍摄剧本里发现了更多线索。

844
00:42:41.240 --> 00:42:47.060
You might have noticed that Kevin doesn't say a single word while he's at Shroot FarMs.
你可能注意到了，凯文在舒鲁特农场时一句话也没说。

845
00:42:47.200 --> 00:42:51.680
In fact, you'll notice he doesn't say anything till after they have left and they're leaving.
事实上，你会发现直到他们离开之后，在路上的时候，他才开口说话。

846
00:42:51.680 --> 00:42:55.280
The whole entire time he's at Shroot Farms, he doesn't say a single word.
他在舒鲁特农场的整个过程中，一个字都没说。

847
00:42:55.560 --> 00:42:56.720
There was a reason.
这是有原因的。

848
00:42:57.460 --> 00:42:58.720
It's in deleted scenes.
在删减片段里有交代。

849
00:42:58.860 --> 00:42:59.680
I want you to hear it.
我想让你听听看。

850
00:43:01.120 --> 00:43:03.800
Okay, guys, I think I'm going to be bad cop and good cop.
好了，伙计们，我想我要同时扮演坏警察和好警察了。

851
00:43:04.040 --> 00:43:06.020
I'm going to be like crazy cop.
我要演得像个疯狂警察。

852
00:43:06.200 --> 00:43:08.740
Dwight Shroot, come out here with your hands up.
德怀特·舒鲁特，举起手来，出来。

853
00:43:10.160 --> 00:43:11.280
I'm so nervous.
我好紧张。

854
00:43:11.580 --> 00:43:12.960
I feel like I'm going to say some.
我觉得我快要说漏嘴了。

855
00:43:16.100 --> 00:43:18.720
Kevin, I'm not going to spin this.
凯文，我不会把这事搞砸的。

856
00:43:19.060 --> 00:43:20.580
I don't think you should say anything.
我觉得你什么都别说比较好。

857
00:43:20.580 --> 00:43:21.400
Yes.
好的。

858
00:43:23.080 --> 00:43:24.580
Mysterious silent guy.
神秘的沉默男。

859
00:43:24.840 --> 00:43:25.140
Yes.
没错。

860
00:43:25.680 --> 00:43:26.460
Starting now.
从现在开始。

861
00:43:28.140 --> 00:43:30.420
I don't remember shooting that.
我不记得拍过那个镜头。

862
00:43:30.660 --> 00:43:33.600
This is dialogue as you guys are walking up to Shroot FarMs.
这是你们走向舒鲁特农场时的对白。

863
00:43:33.740 --> 00:43:34.940
Kevin is having a meltdown.
凯文当时快崩溃了。

864
00:43:35.060 --> 00:43:38.600
He doesn't know how to like coax Dwight or what to say.
他不知道该怎么哄德怀特，也不知道该说什么。

865
00:43:38.620 --> 00:43:40.740
And you guys are just like, don't say a word.
而你们就像是说，别说一个字。

866
00:43:40.920 --> 00:43:41.160
Okay.
好的。

867
00:43:41.540 --> 00:43:42.560
That's pretty great.
那真的很棒。

868
00:43:42.880 --> 00:43:46.060
But that's why when he's like, I don't know.
但这就是为什么当他说，我不知道的时候。

869
00:43:46.340 --> 00:43:47.060
Nothing's working.
什么办法都不管用。

870
00:43:47.240 --> 00:43:48.180
I'll get a skillet.
我去拿个平底锅。

871
00:43:50.080 --> 00:43:54.240
Well, also during the scene, Pam has her very famous line that gets quoted back to me all
嗯，另外在那场戏里，帕姆说了那句非常出名的台词，人们总是拿它来引用我。

872
00:43:54.240 --> 00:43:56.240
the time, which is, po-buddy's nerfict.
那就是，po-buddy's nerfict（倒霉透顶）。

873
00:43:56.500 --> 00:43:57.320
So cute.
太可爱了。

874
00:43:57.920 --> 00:44:00.440
I had not heard this when we were shooting.
拍摄的时候我还没听说过这个词。

875
00:44:00.700 --> 00:44:02.020
I thought Danny made it up.
我以为是丹尼编出来的。

876
00:44:02.400 --> 00:44:04.660
This phrase, po-buddy's nerfict.
这个短语，po-buddy's nerfict。

877
00:44:05.020 --> 00:44:05.460
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

878
00:44:05.820 --> 00:44:11.360
And I remember Danny was like, no, I had this on a doormat when I was growing up.
我记得丹尼当时说，不，我小时候门垫上就有这个。

879
00:44:11.520 --> 00:44:12.640
That's what made him think of it.
那是他想到这个词的原因。

880
00:44:12.780 --> 00:44:13.280
He's like, really?
他说，真的吗？

881
00:44:13.280 --> 00:44:16.320
Yeah, he's like, this has like been around forever.
对，他说，这词儿早就有了。

882
00:44:16.320 --> 00:44:18.000
We did not invent this phrase.
我们并没有发明这个短语。

883
00:44:18.520 --> 00:44:20.520
But people tell me this all the time.
但人们总是跟我提起它。

884
00:44:20.720 --> 00:44:23.900
It's like that phrase, I'm not as think as you drunk I am or whatever.
就像那句，我没你喝醉时想的那么醉，之类的。

885
00:44:24.180 --> 00:44:24.420
Yes.
是的。

886
00:44:24.580 --> 00:44:25.480
No, exactly.
不，没错。

887
00:44:25.700 --> 00:44:26.060
Exactly.
确实。

888
00:44:26.460 --> 00:44:30.020
But I really like this scene because Pam is so laid back.
