00:51:11.520 --> 00:51:15.220
But he clearly tries to break it by throwing it to Robert.
但他显然是想通过扔给罗伯特来把它弄坏。

1056
00:51:15.480 --> 00:51:21.460
But it turns out that it was just an email from JetBlue advertising some specials.
但结果那只是一封捷蓝航空发来的促销邮件。

1057
00:51:21.600 --> 00:51:23.600
It was not the doomsday device.
那根本不是什么末日装置。

1058
00:51:23.960 --> 00:51:25.320
Dwight canceled it.
德怀特取消了它。

1059
00:51:25.320 --> 00:51:29.260
And then he has a really sweet talking head where he explains why.
然后他有一个非常暖心的采访片段，解释了原因。

1060
00:51:29.660 --> 00:51:32.100
He says, you know, these aren't his favorite people.
他说，你知道，这些人并不是他最喜欢的人。

1061
00:51:32.260 --> 00:51:33.500
He wouldn't even call them friends.
他甚至不会称他们为朋友。

1062
00:51:33.520 --> 00:51:39.200
But, you know, to come over and help a guy dig a grave and eat his pie, you know,
但是，你知道，能过来帮一个人挖坟墓还吃他的派，你知道，

1063
00:51:39.460 --> 00:51:40.900
they clearly got to him.
他们显然打动了他。

1064
00:51:41.060 --> 00:51:43.020
He's going to work with them forever, isn't he?
他会和他们一直共事下去，不是吗？

1065
00:51:43.660 --> 00:51:43.880
Yeah.
是啊。

1066
00:51:44.260 --> 00:51:46.580
Well, Pam also had a talking head.
嗯，帕姆也有一个采访片段。

1067
00:51:46.720 --> 00:51:47.480
I remember.
我记得。

1068
00:51:48.080 --> 00:51:49.420
It's really great.
真的很棒。

1069
00:51:49.640 --> 00:51:49.840
Yeah.
是啊。

1070
00:51:49.840 --> 00:51:50.460
It's so sweet.
太贴心了。

1071
00:51:50.660 --> 00:51:51.780
It's in deleted scenes.
那是在删减片段里。

1072
00:51:51.920 --> 00:51:53.140
I want you guys all to hear it.
我想让你们大家都听听。

1073
00:51:54.680 --> 00:51:58.080
Sometimes you just have to let people know they're being heard and valued.
有时候你只需要让人们知道他们的声音被听到了，他们的价值被认可了。

1074
00:51:59.540 --> 00:52:01.520
I don't get how everyone doesn't see that.
我不明白为什么不是每个人都能明白这一点。

1075
00:52:03.000 --> 00:52:03.460
Yeah.
是啊。

1076
00:52:03.660 --> 00:52:07.920
I mean, I feel like the writers saw you do that talking head and loved it.
我是说，我觉得编剧们看到了你做的那个采访片段，然后爱上了它。

1077
00:52:08.020 --> 00:52:13.160
And it's part of the reason why Pam's character has the final talking head of the series.
这也是为什么帕姆的角色拥有全剧最后一个采访片段的原因之一。

1078
00:52:13.440 --> 00:52:14.140
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1079
00:52:14.180 --> 00:52:15.300
That's so sweet, Angela.
那太贴心了，安吉拉。

1080
00:52:15.880 --> 00:52:16.640
It's true.
这是真的。

1081
00:52:16.640 --> 00:52:23.200
When I watched it, I had that same feeling of just, oh, you know, my heart just was so
当我看到那一幕时，我也有同样的感觉，哦，你知道，我的心真的被温暖了，

1082
00:52:23.200 --> 00:52:27.700
warmed by the fact that these people are their co-workers, but they've become this misfit
因为这些人虽然是他们的同事，但他们已经成为了一个古怪的

1083
00:52:27.700 --> 00:52:28.600
family, you know?
大家庭，你知道吗？

1084
00:52:28.880 --> 00:52:33.420
Well, during these talking heads, there's a whole thing going on in the background, which
嗯，在这些采访片段中，背景里发生了一整件事，那就是

1085
00:52:33.420 --> 00:52:37.800
is that Dwight is getting a hat out of the ground.
德怀特正从地里把一顶帽子挖出来。

1086
00:52:37.980 --> 00:52:40.980
This is a hat that the group gave him when they arrived.
这是团队在他们到达时送给他的帽子。

1087
00:52:41.160 --> 00:52:41.520
Yeah.
是啊。

1088
00:52:41.520 --> 00:52:47.180
It's a Sunoco hat, and we got a really cool piece of fan mail about this hat.
那是一顶太阳石油公司的帽子，我们收到了一封关于这顶帽子的非常酷的粉丝来信。

1089
00:52:47.900 --> 00:52:49.420
It comes from Dan R.
它来自丹·R.

1090
00:52:49.620 --> 00:52:52.220
in Westchester, Pennsylvania, who said,
住在宾夕法尼亚州西切斯特，他说，

1091
00:52:52.220 --> 00:52:57.600
When the Doomsday episode first aired in November 2011, I was working at the Sunoco Marcus Hook
当《末日》那一集在2011年11月首次播出时，我正在费城附近的太阳石油公司马库斯胡克炼油厂工作。

1092
00:52:57.600 --> 00:52:59.440
Refinery near Philadelphia, Pennsylvania.
在剧集播出前一天，公司公关总监给所有员工发了邮件，

1093
00:52:59.680 --> 00:53:04.860
And the day before the episode aired, the company communications director emailed all the employees
告诉我们一定要收看《办公室》，因为太阳石油公司在里面特别出镜了。

1094
00:53:04.860 --> 00:53:09.940
telling us to be sure to tune into the office because Sunoco made a special appearance.
每个人都很兴奋地等着收看。

1095
00:53:10.660 --> 00:53:12.480
Everyone was excited to tune in.
但剧集结束后，我们都惊呆了。

1096
00:53:12.620 --> 00:53:14.780
But after the episode ended, we were in shock.
那一集关于可能解雇员工和威胁要关闭分公司的剧情，

1097
00:53:14.780 --> 00:53:21.080
The storyline for the episode with potential firing of employees and threatening a shutdown
真的让我们感同身受，因为当时我们内部也存在类似的

1098
00:53:21.080 --> 00:53:26.400
of the branch, it really hit home because we were having some internal issues that were
问题。

1099
00:53:26.400 --> 00:53:27.820
similar at the time.
这11年多来，我一直很好奇，是不是有人写了这一集

1100
00:53:28.100 --> 00:53:34.160
And I have been wondering all of this time for 11 years plus, did someone write this episode
来影射我们？

1101
00:53:34.160 --> 00:53:37.420
knowing about our company situation or was it a coincidence?
是了解我们公司的状况，还是纯属巧合？

1102
00:53:38.080 --> 00:53:39.360
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1103
00:53:39.960 --> 00:53:41.760
Dan, this is a coincidence.
丹，这纯属巧合。

1104
00:53:42.120 --> 00:53:46.840
This is just, I think, every company all the time, right, deals with these things.
我觉得每家公司一直以来都会遇到这种事，对吧？

1105
00:53:46.940 --> 00:53:52.700
It's why we could do a whole episode about tracking mistakes or about potential branch closures.
这就是为什么我们可以专门做一集来讨论追踪错误或者潜在的分部关闭问题。

1106
00:53:52.880 --> 00:53:54.460
This is kind of corporate stuff.
这算是企业常态吧。

1107
00:53:54.700 --> 00:54:00.580
For anyone who doesn't know, Sunoco is like, has gas stations in Pennsylvania.
对于不知道的人，Sunoco在宾夕法尼亚州有加油站。

1108
00:54:00.580 --> 00:54:06.320
And the idea was simply that they wanted to pick something up as a gift for Dwight on their
当时的想法很简单，他们只是想在路上给德怀特买个礼物。

1109
00:54:06.320 --> 00:54:06.660
way.
顺路。

1110
00:54:06.720 --> 00:54:09.500
And they went to a gas station and they grabbed this hat.
他们去了加油站，顺手拿了这顶帽子。

1111
00:54:09.860 --> 00:54:10.720
That's it.
就是这样。

1112
00:54:11.260 --> 00:54:11.400
Yeah.
没错。

1113
00:54:12.060 --> 00:54:13.340
That was the motivation.
动机就是这样。

1114
00:54:14.100 --> 00:54:16.540
Steve Burgess said we had to get permission to use the hat.
史蒂夫·伯吉斯说我们必须获得使用这顶帽子的许可。

1115
00:54:16.820 --> 00:54:19.900
And Sunoco corporate gave their permission to see the logo.
Sunoco公司同意让我们展示他们的标志。

1116
00:54:20.400 --> 00:54:25.140
And Rainn Wilson even signed a couple of hats that they sent back for people to have.
雷恩·威尔逊甚至还签了几顶他们寄回来的帽子送给别人。

1117
00:54:25.420 --> 00:54:29.160
And all the feedback was just that they loved seeing Dwight wear one of their hats.
所有的反馈都说他们很喜欢看到德怀特戴着他们的帽子。

1118
00:54:29.960 --> 00:54:31.320
It was as simple as that.
事情就是这么简单。

1119
00:54:32.020 --> 00:54:32.180
Yeah.
没错。

1120
00:54:32.740 --> 00:54:34.340
Well, all's well that ends well.
好吧，结局好一切都好。

1121
00:54:34.560 --> 00:54:36.800
The doomsday device is deactivated.
末日装置已经停用了。

1122
00:54:37.380 --> 00:54:42.000
Stanley, however, is now going to have to get our new brandy for his last day of work
不过，斯坦利得为他工作的最后一天去买我们新的白兰地了，

1123
00:54:42.000 --> 00:54:45.360
because he spent the rest of the episode drinking it.
因为他在这一集的剩余时间里都在喝它。

1124
00:54:45.500 --> 00:54:49.120
I saw in the shooting draft that he actually starts pouring some for Phyllis and the two
我在拍摄剧本里看到他其实开始给菲利斯倒酒，

1125
00:54:49.120 --> 00:54:51.020
of them are just sort of giddy in the corner.
他们俩在角落里显得有点晕乎乎的。

1126
00:54:51.500 --> 00:54:51.800
Perfect.
太完美了。

1127
00:54:52.200 --> 00:54:56.040
Well, thank you guys so much for listening and sending in your questions and comments.
非常感谢大家收听并发送你们的问题和评论。

1128
00:54:56.040 --> 00:54:59.940
Thank you to Steve Burgess once again for giving us behind the scenes details.
再次感谢史蒂夫·伯吉斯为我们提供幕后细节。

1129
00:55:00.280 --> 00:55:03.340
And thank you, Dani Chun, for emailing with me as well.
也感谢丹妮·春与我进行邮件沟通。

1130
00:55:03.800 --> 00:55:04.320
Yes.
是的。

1131
00:55:04.320 --> 00:55:09.620
We hope you guys have a great rest of the week and we'll be back next week to chat with you.
希望大家这周剩下的时间过得愉快，我们下周回来再和大家聊天。

1132
00:55:10.040 --> 00:55:11.240
Sam, hiccups?
萨姆，打嗝了吗？

1133
00:55:12.180 --> 00:55:13.520
Unfortunately, going strong.
不幸的是，还在持续。

1134
00:55:13.900 --> 00:55:15.380
Oh, no, Sam.
噢，不，萨姆。

1135
00:55:15.720 --> 00:55:16.140
I know.
我知道。

1136
00:55:16.960 --> 00:55:17.480
All right.
好吧。

1137
00:55:17.740 --> 00:55:18.380
All right.
好吧。

1138
00:55:18.700 --> 00:55:23.460
Well, if you guys have any remedies for hiccups, DM us and we'll see you here next.
如果你们有什么治打嗝的偏方，私信我们，我们下期见。

1139
00:55:23.460 --> 00:55:24.560
Oh, no, Sam.
噢，不，萨姆。

1140
00:55:24.660 --> 00:55:28.840
I mean, I really hope that Sam doesn't still have the hiccups by the time this episode comes
我是说，我真希望这集播出的时候萨姆已经不打嗝了。

1141
00:55:28.840 --> 00:55:29.100
out.
出来。

1142
00:55:29.300 --> 00:55:30.040
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1143
00:55:30.040 --> 00:55:31.000
I hope not, too.
我也希望如此。

1144
00:55:31.260 --> 00:55:31.580
All right.
好吧。

1145
00:55:31.700 --> 00:55:33.460
Well, you guys have a great rest of the week.
祝大家这周剩下的时间过得愉快。

1146
00:55:33.620 --> 00:55:34.560
We'll see you next week.
我们下周见。

1147
00:55:34.740 --> 00:55:35.300
See you then.
到时候见。

1148
00:55:40.470 --> 00:55:42.350
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

